  "name": "Creality K2 / K2 Plus / K2 Pro toolhead (unicorn nozzle, rear 4020 blower with duct under head, front cover)",
  "provenance": "Creality K2 / K2 Plus / K2 Pro toolhead (unicorn nozzle, rear 4020 blower with duct under head, front cover) Confidence: medium. Sources: https://www.printables.com/model/1415219 (Mike Sinkovsky, 'Creality K2 toolhead (CAD model)', K2-toolhead.stp, reverse-engineered: hotend, model-fan module, front cover, carriage, belt tips); https://www.printables.com/model/1408748 (same author, K2 hotend CAD). Measured on Mike Sinkovsky's reverse-engineered K2 toolhead STEP (model axes = printer axes, front cover at -Y, carriage/rails at +Y); tip = lowest point of 'unicorn-nozzle'. The part-cooling (model-fan) module has a flat underside at 4.1 mm spanning x +-24, y -5.5..+53.5 (duct runs from the rear 4020 blower under the head to the nozzle); the front cover lower edge is also at 4.1 mm (y -9.9..-5.8). This 50 x 64 mm flat plane 4.1 mm above the tip is the binding constraint in every direction. Same toolhead across K2 / K2 Plus / K2 Pro (shared K2-series hotend and model-fan module); K2 SE assumed same. Gantry not in the CAD: the X belts pass through the carriage at 25.2-33.2 mm (and 65-73 mm); the gantry z is set to 25.0 with the carriage y span. Nozzle: land radius 0.40 mm, 37.4-degree cone to Z=2.60, then the nozzle parts as recorded. Gantry: X beam underside 25.00 mm above the tip, Y 9.0..50.0, every X. Converted by scripts/nonplanar_heads/open_heads.py from research/head-envelopes/creality-k2.json (2026-10-13). Nozzle-tip frame +X right, +Y rear, +Z up, mm. Body axial/lateral margins 0.3 mm. Not calibrated.",
